    "observed_dialogue": [
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.67",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "the biggest frustrations that people found with regard to personal preferences were um something that you you mentioned earlier , uh remote controls are often lost in the room ,",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.68",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "it's a slipping down the back of the sofa type of thing , uh",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.69",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "fifty percent were were particularly frustrated by that .",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.A.dialog-act.s9553330.48",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "and s maybe we we should look at also like the buttons whe whether they are like soft or little hard",
        "participant": "MEO015",
        "role": "UI"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.A.dialog-act.s9553330.49",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "because they are times when the buttons tend to be a bit hard after uh continuous use <disfmarker> usage and all that .",
        "participant": "MEO015",
        "role": "UI"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.C.dialog-act.s9553330.83",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "Yeah .",
        "participant": "MEE014",
        "role": "ID"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.70",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "Uh thirty four percent of people take <disfmarker> said they take too much time to learn to use",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.71",
        "meeting_id": "ES2004b",
        "text": "and I think that ties in with the um the previous finding of people only using ten percent of the buttons ,",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.66",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME",
        "text": "Um and possibly we can also cut back on cost if we don't have so many functions actually on the remote control . Um"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.A.dialog-act.s9553330.47",
        "participant": "MEO015",
        "role": "UI",
        "text": "if you ask me personally , I would make uh flip-top with a trendy uh uh design"
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.A.dialog-act.s9553330.50",
        "participant": "MEO015",
        "role": "UI",
        "text": "So in overall a simple and uh user-friendly design ."
      },
      {
        "da_id": "ES2004b.D.dialog-act.s9553330.72",
        "participant": "FEE016",
        "role": "ME",
        "text": "they just can't be bothered to learn about the other functions ."
      }
    ],
